  "articleBody": "Planning a wall tile update in your bathroom sounds simple until you realize how much happens behind the surface. A great tile job depends entirely on the wall beneath it, and skipping basic checks can leave you with loose tiles or cracked grout later.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide\n\nBefore hiring an installer, find out how they handle prep work:\n- Will you flatten and plumb the studs before hanging tile backer?\n- What mortar or adhesive is specified for this exact tile type?\n- How do you handle movement joints where walls meet floors and corners?\n- If the house was built before 1978, do you follow EPA lead-safe work practices when disturbing painted surfaces?\n\nTile absorption ratings, tile weight, and moisture exposure determine whether standard mastic or a modified thin-set mortar is required. Large-format tiles demand an exceptionally flat plane to prevent lippage, while changes in plane require flexible sealant rather than rigid grout to prevent cracking.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n\nIf you find hidden mold, soft framing, or walls that are significantly bowed, bringing in a full-service remodeling contractor saves time and protects your home. At HH Remodeling LLC, owner Abraham Becerra provides hands-on oversight for drywall, framing, and tile installation across the Denver area. Call 303-505-0866 or email Hhremodelingllc1986.ab@gmail.com to discuss your bathroom wall tile project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}